2304 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 933 0 R
/E (Eco Wrap will finance its early-stage operations with a $600,000 bank loan, issued in January 2026 at a 3% interest rate over five years. The repayment structure is fixed and predictable: Eco Wrap will pay $120,000 in principal each year, alongside a consistent $18,000 in annual interest, resulting in a total interest expense of $90,000 over the full loan period. The loan balance decreases steadily from $600,000 in 2026 to $0 by the end of 2030. Eco Wrap will allocate a portion of its yearly operating income to cover these repayments, ensuring that the loan is fully retired on schedule while preserving enough cash flow for reinvestment into manufacturing, technology development, and expansion.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
2305 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 933 0 R
/E (For Eco Wrap, 75% of the profit will be retained by the company. 5% of the profits will be withdrawn by the owners, and another 2.5% for loans. The final 17.5% of profits will go to shareholders and investors)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
